### Where this node lives, and whether it still lives here.

# A term (a name that starts with `-`) goes on with a line that has to stay one
# line and is wider than a line of a catalog.
-dwelling-would-be-one = would be one
-dwelling-anywhere-this = anywhere, this

dwelling-made-at = made at
dwelling-unpacked-at = unpacked at
dwelling-moved-to = said to have moved to
dwelling-found-at = first opened by this client at

dwelling-writing = writing { $file }
dwelling-putting-in-place = putting { $file } in place
dwelling-resolving = resolving { $dir }

dwelling-elsewhere = this node was { $how } { $was },
    and it is now at { $now }.
    If the directory was moved or renamed, that is all this is. If it was
    copied and the one it came from still runs, this is one name in two
    places, and each will contradict the other's record. Once only one of
    them is left, say so here: { $settle }
    .keyword = home

dwelling-unread-moment = a moment that could not be read
dwelling-unread-file = a file whose name could not be read

dwelling-packed = this node was packed for moving at { $at }, into { $into }.
    It lives wherever that file was unpacked. Running it here too { -dwelling-would-be-one }
    name in two places, so nothing in { $home } will act as it.

    If the move was abandoned and that file was never unpacked { -dwelling-anywhere-this }
    puts it back: { $undo }

dwelling-unmarking = removing the mark that this node was packed
